{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":71999,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"b5b33c8c-fe18-5b2d-a468-8da41534161e","total_cost_usd":0.5502079999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9222,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7240,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7240,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3663,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003748,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7240,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9222,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.54646,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-i1-reviewer-fable-40\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:ce7daed01bb0fa178e26\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\",\"bounded_statement\":\"The selected result (exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U on 12 leaf records, U = 35.0, p = 0.004329) enters each of the six independent units (plants, per plant_id) twice into a rank-sum procedure whose exact null distribution treats every entered value as an independent observation; the reported significance at p < 0.01 is attributable to this repeated entry, since an exact Mann-Whitney test at the authorized plant level (3 vs 3 plant means, which show perfect group separation) cannot yield a two-sided p below 0.1.\",\"root_cause\":\"workflow/analysis.py pools all leaf-level rows per amendment group in collect_groups (appending record conductance keyed only by amendment) and passes these pooled lists of 6 leaf values per group directly to scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu with method=\\\"exact\\\", so each plant's two correlated leaf readings are counted as two independent observations, inflating the effective sample size from 3 vs 3 plants to 6 vs 6 rows and deflating the exact p-value from a minimum attainable 0.1 to 0.004329.\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description designates plant_id as the independent-unit column and states each plant appears in two rows, so the 12 rows represent only 6 independent units (3 per amendment group).\",\"observed_value\":\"6 plants, 2 leaf rows each, 3 plants per group\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one porometer reading taken on a single leaf of one potted sunflower\\nIndependent unit column: plant_id\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"The twelve rows therefore come from six plants, three per amendment group, with\\ntwo leaf readings per plant.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow pools conductance values keyed only by amendment group, appending every leaf row as a separate observation with no aggregation to the plant level.\",\"observed_value\":\"6 leaf values per group entered as 6 observations\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":28,\"end_line\":31,\"quoted_text\":\"for record in records:\\n        group = record[\\\"amendment\\\"]\\n        conductance[group].append(float(record[\\\"conductance_mmol_m2_s\\\"]))\\n        plants[group].add(record[\\\"plant_id\\\"])\"}]},{\"description\":\"The pooled leaf-level lists are passed directly to an exact Mann-Whitney U test, a row-independent procedure whose exact null distribution assumes all 12 entered values are exchangeable independent observations under the null.\",\"observed_value\":\"mannwhitneyu on 6 vs 6 leaf rows, method='exact'\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":99,\"end_line\":104,\"quoted_text\":\"u_stat, p_value = mannwhitneyu(\\n        conductance[\\\"biochar\\\"],\\n        conductance[\\\"control\\\"],\\n        alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\",\\n        method=\\\"exact\\\",\\n    )\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result reports the leaf-level test as the statistical conclusion, with p = 0.004329 derived from n = 6 vs 6 rows; this p equals 4/924, the two-sided exact tail probability for U >= 35 with 6-vs-6 independent observations, confirming the test's sample size was the row count, not the plant count.\",\"observed_value\":\"U = 35.0, p = 0.004329 = 4/C(12,6)\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 leaf records (6 biochar vs 6 control): U = 35.0, p = 0.004329, median conductance 160.95 vs 115.15 mmol m-2 s-1.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":14,\"quoted_text\":\"Each leaf record was entered as one observation and the two amendment groups\\nwere compared with a two-sided Mann-Whitney U test evaluated against the exact\\nnull distribution (no tied conductance values occur in the file).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The two leaf readings from each plant are tightly clustered relative to between-plant spread (e.g., PL-01: 96.2 and 99.8; PL-06: 179.4 and 186.0), showing within-plant dependence, so the two rows per plant are not independent draws and their repeated entry genuinely inflates evidence. Aggregating to plant means gives control plants 98.0, 115.15, 132.3 vs biochar plants 135.95, 160.95, 182.7; a 3-vs-3 exact two-sided Mann-Whitney test on these has minimum attainable p = 2/C(6,3) = 0.1, so the reported p < 0.01 cannot be reproduced at the independent-unit level.\",\"observed_value\":\"plant-level exact two-sided p = 0.1 (minimum possible for 3 vs 3) vs reported 0.004329\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"PL-01,control,lower,96.2\\nPL-01,control,upper,99.8\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"PL-06,biochar,lower,179.4\\nPL-06,biochar,upper,186.0\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report transparently discloses that leaf records were entered as individual observations and reports the true number of plants (3 per group) alongside the leaf-record count in the group summary table, so the unit inflation is not concealed; however, disclosure does not make the row-independent procedure valid for correlated within-plant rows.\",\"observed_value\":\"table reports 'leaf records' = 6 and 'plants' = 3 per group\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"| amendment | leaf records | plants | mean | median |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| biochar | 6 | 3 | 159.87 | 160.95 |\\n| control | 6 | 3 | 115.15 | 115.15 |\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"Each leaf record was entered as one observation and the two amendment groups\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow does track distinct plant identities per group via a set, showing the analyst was aware of the plant structure, and the exact-method choice is internally consistent for the data as entered (no ties); this shows careful execution of the chosen procedure, but the chosen procedure still treats dependent rows as independent.\",\"observed_value\":\"plants tracked as sets of plant_id per group\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"    plants = {name: set() for name in GROUP_ORDER}\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to defeat the finding three ways. (1) Alternative independent unit: could leaves be the independent unit? No — data-description.md explicitly names plant_id as the independent-unit column, and treatment (amendment) is assigned at the pot/plant level in a single run, so leaves within a plant share both treatment assignment and plant-level variation; the data confirm within-plant clustering (paired leaf readings differ by 3.6–8.7 units while between-plant spread within groups is ~34–47 units). (2) Robustness of the conclusion: I recomputed the test at the plant level. Plant means are 98.0, 115.15, 132.3 (control) vs 135.95, 160.95, 182.7 (biochar); with perfect separation the exact two-sided Mann-Whitney p for 3 vs 3 is 2/20 = 0.1, the minimum attainable, so the reported p = 0.004329 and any claim of significance at conventional thresholds cannot be reproduced without the repeated per-plant entries. (3) Arithmetic check: 4/C(12,6) = 4/924 = 0.004329, exactly matching the reported p, confirming the test was run on 12 rows (6 vs 6), not 6 plants. All three checks confirm rather than falsify the issue.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-i1-reviewer-fable-40","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:ce7daed01bb0fa178e26","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"The selected result (exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U on 12 leaf records, U = 35.0, p = 0.004329) enters each of the six independent units (plants, per plant_id) twice into a rank-sum procedure whose exact null distribution treats every entered value as an independent observation; the reported significance at p < 0.01 is attributable to this repeated entry, since an exact Mann-Whitney test at the authorized plant level (3 vs 3 plant means, which show perfect group separation) cannot yield a two-sided p below 0.1.","root_cause":"workflow/analysis.py pools all leaf-level rows per amendment group in collect_groups (appending record conductance keyed only by amendment) and passes these pooled lists of 6 leaf values per group directly to scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu with method=\"exact\", so each plant's two correlated leaf readings are counted as two independent observations, inflating the effective sample size from 3 vs 3 plants to 6 vs 6 rows and deflating the exact p-value from a minimum attainable 0.1 to 0.004329.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description designates plant_id as the independent-unit column and states each plant appears in two rows, so the 12 rows represent only 6 independent units (3 per amendment group).","observed_value":"6 plants, 2 leaf rows each, 3 plants per group","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":9,"end_line":10,"quoted_text":"One row is: one porometer reading taken on a single leaf of one potted sunflower\nIndependent unit column: plant_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":22,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"The twelve rows therefore come from six plants, three per amendment group, with\ntwo leaf readings per plant."}]},{"description":"The workflow pools conductance values keyed only by amendment group, appending every leaf row as a separate observation with no aggregation to the plant level.","observed_value":"6 leaf values per group entered as 6 observations","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":28,"end_line":31,"quoted_text":"for record in records:\n        group = record[\"amendment\"]\n        conductance[group].append(float(record[\"conductance_mmol_m2_s\"]))\n        plants[group].add(record[\"plant_id\"])"}]},{"description":"The pooled leaf-level lists are passed directly to an exact Mann-Whitney U test, a row-independent procedure whose exact null distribution assumes all 12 entered values are exchangeable independent observations under the null.","observed_value":"mannwhitneyu on 6 vs 6 leaf rows, method='exact'","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":99,"end_line":104,"quoted_text":"u_stat, p_value = mannwhitneyu(\n        conductance[\"biochar\"],\n        conductance[\"control\"],\n        alternative=\"two-sided\",\n        method=\"exact\",\n    )"}]},{"description":"The selected result reports the leaf-level test as the statistical conclusion, with p = 0.004329 derived from n = 6 vs 6 rows; this p equals 4/924, the two-sided exact tail probability for U >= 35 with 6-vs-6 independent observations, confirming the test's sample size was the row count, not the plant count.","observed_value":"U = 35.0, p = 0.004329 = 4/C(12,6)","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":27,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 leaf records (6 biochar vs 6 control): U = 35.0, p = 0.004329, median conductance 160.95 vs 115.15 mmol m-2 s-1."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":12,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"Each leaf record was entered as one observation and the two amendment groups\nwere compared with a two-sided Mann-Whitney U test evaluated against the exact\nnull distribution (no tied conductance values occur in the file)."}]},{"description":"The two leaf readings from each plant are tightly clustered relative to between-plant spread (e.g., PL-01: 96.2 and 99.8; PL-06: 179.4 and 186.0), showing within-plant dependence, so the two rows per plant are not independent draws and their repeated entry genuinely inflates evidence. Aggregating to plant means gives control plants 98.0, 115.15, 132.3 vs biochar plants 135.95, 160.95, 182.7; a 3-vs-3 exact two-sided Mann-Whitney test on these has minimum attainable p = 2/C(6,3) = 0.1, so the reported p < 0.01 cannot be reproduced at the independent-unit level.","observed_value":"plant-level exact two-sided p = 0.1 (minimum possible for 3 vs 3) vs reported 0.004329","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":3,"quoted_text":"PL-01,control,lower,96.2\nPL-01,control,upper,99.8"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":12,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"PL-06,biochar,lower,179.4\nPL-06,biochar,upper,186.0"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The report transparently discloses that leaf records were entered as individual observations and reports the true number of plants (3 per group) alongside the leaf-record count in the group summary table, so the unit inflation is not concealed; however, disclosure does not make the row-independent procedure valid for correlated within-plant rows.","observed_value":"table reports 'leaf records' = 6 and 'plants' = 3 per group","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":18,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"| amendment | leaf records | plants | mean | median |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| biochar | 6 | 3 | 159.87 | 160.95 |\n| control | 6 | 3 | 115.15 | 115.15 |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":12,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"Each leaf record was entered as one observation and the two amendment groups"}]},{"description":"The workflow does track distinct plant identities per group via a set, showing the analyst was aware of the plant structure, and the exact-method choice is internally consistent for the data as entered (no ties); this shows careful execution of the chosen procedure, but the chosen procedure still treats dependent rows as independent.","observed_value":"plants tracked as sets of plant_id per group","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":27,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"    plants = {name: set() for name in GROUP_ORDER}"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to defeat the finding three ways. (1) Alternative independent unit: could leaves be the independent unit? No — data-description.md explicitly names plant_id as the independent-unit column, and treatment (amendment) is assigned at the pot/plant level in a single run, so leaves within a plant share both treatment assignment and plant-level variation; the data confirm within-plant clustering (paired leaf readings differ by 3.6–8.7 units while between-plant spread within groups is ~34–47 units). (2) Robustness of the conclusion: I recomputed the test at the plant level. Plant means are 98.0, 115.15, 132.3 (control) vs 135.95, 160.95, 182.7 (biochar); with perfect separation the exact two-sided Mann-Whitney p for 3 vs 3 is 2/20 = 0.1, the minimum attainable, so the reported p = 0.004329 and any claim of significance at conventional thresholds cannot be reproduced without the repeated per-plant entries. (3) Arithmetic check: 4/C(12,6) = 4/924 = 0.004329, exactly matching the reported p, confirming the test was run on 12 rows (6 vs 6), not 6 plants. All three checks confirm rather than falsify the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":32245,"ttft_stream_ms":1609,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":72915,"uuid":"d7e9a353-48c4-4fcd-8d3a-2ad0449442f4"}
